specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/001-template-drift-census-and-baseline/tasks.md:109:  RETURN exactly one line: [T004-<LANE>] DONE - <number of rows> rows
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/001-template-drift-census-and-baseline/tasks.md:114:- [ ] T005 Check lane coverage (`scratch/ledger/coverage.txt`). Run this block from `$WORKTREE`. It writes one line per lane.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/001-template-drift-census-and-baseline/tasks.md:146:- [ ] T006 Reduce to verified rows (`scratch/ledger/candidates.jsonl`, `ledger.jsonl`, `dropped.jsonl`, `unsafe.jsonl`). Run this script from `$WORKTREE`. Verify: `wc -l "$PHASE"/scratch/ledger/{ledger,dropped,unsafe}.jsonl` prints three counts, and `ledger.jsonl` is not empty.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/001-template-drift-census-and-baseline/tasks.md:164:- [ ] T007 Check the five confirmed defects are in the ledger (no file). Verify: each of these five commands prints a number of at least 1, and the first prints at least 18, one for each of the 18 exact lines in `plan.md` section 3.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/001-template-drift-census-and-baseline/tasks.md:174:  A missing defect is added by the conductor as a row in the frozen schema, using the locator in `plan.md` section 3, then T006's reproduce check is run on that row alone.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/001-template-drift-census-and-baseline/tasks.md:176:- [ ] T008 Build the hint list (`scratch/baseline/hints-v2.2.txt`). Run from `$WORKTREE`. Verify: `wc -l < "$PHASE/scratch/baseline/hints-v2.2.txt"` prints a number above 50, and `ls specs/zz-bench-hints 2>&1` reports no such directory.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/001-template-drift-census-and-baseline/tasks.md:188:- [ ] T009 Run the baseline three times (`scratch/runs/T009-1.txt` to `T009-3.txt`, `scratch/baseline/runs.jsonl`). Runs are serial. Before each run, save `git status --porcelain` to `scratch/baseline/status-before-<n>.txt` and run `date +%s > "$PHASE/scratch/runs/T009-<n>.t0"`. Dispatch this brief, saved as `scratch/briefs/T009-<n>.txt`, as one Task call with the plan's dispatch rule, writing to `scratch/runs/T009-<n>.txt`, then run `date +%s > "$PHASE/scratch/runs/T009-<n>.t1"`. Verify: `for n in 1 2 3; do test -s "$PHASE/scratch/runs/T009-$n.txt" && test -s "$PHASE/scratch/runs/T009-$n.t0" && test -s "$PHASE/scratch/baseline/status-before-$n.txt" && echo "run-$n recorded"; done` prints `run-1 recorded`, `run-2 recorded` and `run-3 recorded`.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/001-template-drift-census-and-baseline/tasks.md:220:- [ ] T010 Measure each run, then delete its track (`scratch/baseline/baseline.json`). After each run, before the next one starts, run this from `$WORKTREE` with `N` set to the run number and `T0=$(cat "$PHASE/scratch/runs/T009-$N.t0")`. Verify: `jq '.runs | length' "$PHASE/scratch/baseline/baseline.json"` prints `3` after the third run.
