specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/001-template-drift-census-and-baseline/tasks.md:269:- [ ] T012 Apply review findings (`scratch/ledger/ledger.jsonl`, `goal.md`). For each finding, fix the row, add a NEW row through T006's reproduce check or record in `goal.md` section 4 why it was not applied. Write one line per finding in `goal.md` section 4 as `T012-APPLIED <finding id>` or `T012-RECORDED <finding id> <reason>`. Write no T012 line when T011 is `NO FINDINGS`. Verify: `test "$(grep -cE '^(P0|P1|P2) ' "$PHASE/scratch/review/T011.txt")" -eq "$(grep -cE '^T012-(APPLIED|RECORDED) ' "$PHASE/goal.md")" && echo T012_COUNTS_MATCH` prints `T012_COUNTS_MATCH`.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/001-template-drift-census-and-baseline/tasks.md:271:- [ ] T013 Write `scratch/baseline/baseline.md` (`scratch/baseline/baseline.md`). One table of the three runs and their five metrics, then the minimum and maximum of each metric. Write one row per run as `| <run> | <strict_passed> | <leftover_hints> | <missing_anchors> | <out_of_scope_writes> | <seconds> |`, for example `| 1 | 1 | 87 | 0 | 0 | 420 |`. Verify: `grep -c '^| [123] |' "$PHASE/scratch/baseline/baseline.md"` prints `3`.
