specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/005-weak-model-authoring-card/spec.md:57:- Phase 003 is a prerequisite. On the post-003 tree the five core templates are stamped `v2.3` and carry `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:` tokens, and the validator applies the Draft lifecycle to them.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/005-weak-model-authoring-card/spec.md:58:- Phase 004 is a prerequisite. On the post-004 tree each template section carries a fill note, and the four `Task Format` declarations are stable.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/005-weak-model-authoring-card/spec.md:70:<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-context -->
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/005-weak-model-authoring-card/spec.md:74:<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/005-weak-model-authoring-card/spec.md:78:The router sends four authoring intents to `references/templates/template-guide.md`, a 1,200-line guide. A weak model that loads it writes less, not more: it samples the guide and copies the nearest example. The guide also mixes template-authoring rules with packet-authoring rules, so a model that only needs to fill a scaffold reads rules about `.tmpl` files it must not touch.
