specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/spec.md:3:description: "Bring every speckit command and every doc-authoring agent in line with the templates, the placeholder gate and the authoring card that phases 2 to 5 change, then regenerate every runtime mirror from those sources."
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/spec.md:12:<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.2 -->
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/spec.md:22:Phases 2 to 5 change the templates, the placeholder gate and the authoring guidance. Every speckit command and every agent that writes or checks spec docs still describes the old rules, so a weak writer follows stale text even after the templates improve. This phase audits the whole command and agent surface against six checks, applies 27 exact text rows by script, and regenerates every runtime mirror from the corrected sources.
