specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/spec.md:78:A speckit command tells a writer where to find authoring guidance, how a placeholder is treated and which files a packet holds. Six of those statements are now wrong or incomplete, and the same wrong text is copied into seven runtime trees. A weak model reads the command, follows the stale line and produces the defect that phases 2 to 5 just fixed in the templates.
