specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:2:title: "Feature Specification: Phase 3: versioned-placeholder-gate"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:3:description: "Convert every authoring hint in the core templates to a value token stamped v2.3, and make the validator treat an unfilled token as a warning while the packet is a Draft and as an error afterwards, for v2.3 docs only."
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:5:  - "versioned placeholder gate"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:6:  - "phase 3 versioned placeholder gate"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:8:  - "template v2.3 stamp"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:12:<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.2 -->
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:13:# Feature Specification: Phase 3: versioned-placeholder-gate
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:22:A fresh Level 2 scaffold holds 97 bracketed hint occurrences and `validate.sh --strict` still prints `RESULT: PASSED` on it, so a weak model can leave every hint in place and pass. This phase turns each hint of the five core templates into a `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: ...]` token, stamps those templates v2.3, and teaches both validator implementations that an unfilled token is a warning while the spec status is Draft and an error at any other status. A doc without the v2.3 stamp keeps its old verdict exactly.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:24:**Key Decisions**: the existing token is the only grammar, and the template stamp, not a flag, decides which docs the new lifecycle covers.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:26:**Critical Dependencies**: phase 2 closed, because this is the first phase to edit `templates/core`, and the launch preconditions in `../spec.md` section 3.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:29:<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:41:| **Predecessor** | 002-template-and-example-defect-repair |
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:42:| **Successor** | 004-template-section-fill-guidance |
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:43:| **Handoff Criteria** | The failing-first test passes and goes red under each mutation, recursive strict counts over `specs/` match before and after, and the five core templates hold 214 value tokens, the kept texts listed in `tasks.md` T011 and the v2.3 stamp |
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:44:<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:48:<!-- ANCHOR:phase-context -->
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:51:This is **Phase 3** of the Make system-spec-kit templates and authoring docs followable by a DeepSeek V4.1 Flash agent swarm specification.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:53:**Scope Boundary**: Edits land only in the files listed in section 3 under `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/`, plus this phase folder and the throwaway track `specs/zz-bench-gate/`, which the smoke test creates and deletes. No other template, example, reference or script changes.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:57:- Phase 2 is closed. It leaves `templates/core` untouched, so this phase starts from the original hints.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:58:- Phase 1 produced `../001-template-drift-census-and-baseline/scratch/ledger/ledger.jsonl` and `../001-template-drift-census-and-baseline/scratch/baseline/suite-start.txt`.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:61:- The five templates `core/spec.md.tmpl`, `core/plan.md.tmpl`, `core/tasks.md.tmpl`, `core/implementation-summary.md.tmpl` and `addons/acceptance-criteria.md.tmpl` converted to value tokens and stamped v2.3.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:62:- The lifecycle in the orchestrator function `validatePlaceholders` and in the shell rule `rules/check-placeholders.sh`, built and tested together.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:63:- `runtime/cli/tests/placeholder-token-gate.vitest.ts`, which fails before the change and passes after it.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:65:- Five corrected lines in `references/templates/template-guide.md` and a lifecycle section in `references/validation/validation-rules.md`.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:69:<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-context -->
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:73:<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:77:Phase 1 measured a fresh Level 2 scaffold at 87 distinct hint strings and 97 occurrences, and strict validation passes it. The validator only flags the `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:` token, and the templates do not use that token for their hints, so nothing tells a weak model, or the validator, that a hint is unfilled. Turning on a blanket error would break every existing packet and every external repo, so the gate has to apply to new docs only.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:80:A packet scaffolded after this phase cannot reach a non-Draft status with an unfilled hint, and no packet written before it changes its verdict.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:81:<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:85:<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:86:## 3. SCOPE
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:88:### In Scope
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:89:- Convert every bracketed hint in the five templates to `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: <hint text>]` with a script, and stamp the templates v2.3.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:92:- Regenerate the scaffold golden snapshot, because it renders these templates.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:93:- Update the template manifest versions so the version parity test keeps passing.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/spec.md:94:- Fix the five `[PLACEHOLDER]` lines in `template-guide.md` and describe the lifecycle in `validation-rules.md`.
