specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/002-template-and-example-defect-repair/tasks.md:412:- [ ] T014 Compare the spec-kit suite with the phase 1 start (`scratch/suite-end.txt`). Run the first block. It takes several minutes. Then run the second block. Verify: the second block prints `SUITE_MATCH`. A match means the `Test Files` lines, the `Tests` lines and the final `exit=` line are identical in both files. Durations and start times are not compared. When it prints `SUITE_DIFF`, read the diff it shows and mark this task `[B]`. A line that appears only in the end file and starts with `FAIL` names a new failing test. Rerun the first block once before you decide, because a flaky test can differ between runs. A second diff blocks the phase.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/002-template-and-example-defect-repair/tasks.md:430:- [ ] T015 Frontier review of the diff (`scratch/review/T015.txt`). Read `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/SKILL.md` first. Use its read-only invocation with the `gpt-6-luna` model, as phase 1 did. Write the brief with the first block and send it with the second block. The reply lands in `scratch/review/T015.txt`. Verify: every line of the file matches `^(P0|P1|P2) ` or the file holds the single line `NO FINDINGS`. Check it with `grep -cvE '^(P0|P1|P2) |^NO FINDINGS$' "$PHASE/scratch/review/T015.txt"`, which must print `0`.
