specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/002-template-and-example-defect-repair/tasks.md:462:- [ ] T016 Apply the review findings (`scratch/review/T016.txt`, `scratch/briefs/T016-<n>.txt`, `goal.md`). Do not edit any file a finding names by hand. For each `P0`, `P1` or `P2` line, write a brief with the Worker Brief Skeleton in `plan.md` section AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL. Put the finding's file under ALLOWED WRITE PATHS and the finding line in the TASK section. Dispatch it with the Task tool as described under Dispatch Command in the same section, with the brief at `scratch/briefs/T016-<n>.txt` and the reply at `scratch/runs/T016-<n>.txt`. At most 3 Task calls in one message, and never two that write the same file. Write `APPLIED <file>` to `scratch/review/T016.txt` after the dispatch. Write `RECORDED <file>` instead when the dispatch failed or the finding asks for a change outside the files the rows name, and raise it to the operator. Write every finding in `goal.md` section 4. Then rerun T012, T013 and T014. A `P2` finding is fixed by a worker or recorded with the reason it was not fixed. When T015 holds `NO FINDINGS`, run `: > "$PHASE/scratch/review/T016.txt"` and skip the dispatches. Verify: the block below prints `COUNTS_MATCH`.
