specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:12:<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.2 -->
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:13:# Feature Specification: Phase 4: template-section-fill-guidance
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:22:Phase 003 turns every core hint into a value token. A token still does not tell a weak model what to write. This phase puts one imperative instruction below every section heading, with a good and a weak example, so the model copies a standard instead of inventing one. It also aligns the 14 drifted examples a model imitates and adds two guards so the guidance cannot rot.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:24:**Key Decisions**: the guidance is an HTML comment below the heading, and the example drift guard delegates anchor comparison to the template contract.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:26:**Critical Dependencies**: phase 002 must be closed, because it repairs the 18 leaked example descriptions and the drift guard's description rules pass only on that tree. Phase 003 must be closed, because every locator is written in both the pre-token and post-token form.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:29:<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:41:| **Predecessor** | 003-versioned-placeholder-gate |
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:43:| **Handoff Criteria** | Every core section has one fill line, the fill test prints `16 passed`, the golden test prints `12 passed`, the drift guard prints `EXAMPLE_DRIFT_OK`, and `goal.md` section 4 names what phases 005, 006 and 007 may assume |
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:44:<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->
