specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:168:- **SC-001**: A weak model that opens a scaffold sees one imperative action and one good and one weak example for every section it must fill.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:169:- **SC-002**: A filled section leaves no residue that the placeholder gate counts as an unfilled placeholder.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:170:- **SC-003**: A maintainer who edits one example anchor can detect the drift with one command that prints one line per failure.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:171:<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:175:<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:181:| Dependency | The template contract keeps the required and optional anchor lists | The drift guard reports false drift | The guard calls the contract, so it inherits any change instead of hard-coding a list |
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:183:| Risk | The fill text is too long for a table cell and breaks the template | A scaffold renders broken | Every line is one physical line and the fill test renders all 16 documents |
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:184:| Risk | A snapshot regeneration hides a real regression | A broken render passes | The fill test and the anchor count run separately from the snapshot diff, and the frontier review reads the rendered sections |
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:185:<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:206:- Empty input: a template with no `## ` heading fails the fill test with a named message rather than passing silently.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:212:- A section that exists only at one level: the fill line sits inside the same gate as the heading, so it renders only at that level.
