specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:235:| R-003 | The drift guard treats an optional section as drift | M | M | The guard reads the contract, which marks optional anchors |
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:237:| R-005 | A weak model copies the weak example | H | L | The weak example carries a `WEAK:` label and the instruction names the failure |
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/spec.md:245:**As a** DeepSeek V4.1 Flash worker, **I want** one imperative instruction and one good and one weak example under each heading, **so that** I copy a standard instead of inventing one.
