specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:48:- [ ] T001 Check that phases 1, 4 and 5 closed (no file). Run the block below. Verify: it prints `LEDGER_OK`, `CARD_OK`, `CARD_SYNC_OK` and `EXAMPLE_DRIFT_OK`. When a line is missing, write `MISSING <name>` in `goal.md` section 4 and continue, because T006 records each dependent row as `SKIP-MISSING` and the phase can still close with that row recorded.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:55:  test -x "$S/runtime/cli/spec/check-example-drift.sh" && echo EXAMPLE_DRIFT_OK
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:60:- [ ] T003 Record the start state (`goal.md`, `scratch/status-start.txt`, `scratch/suite-before.txt`, `scratch/doctor-before.json`). Run the block below. Write the hash `git rev-parse` prints into the `Phase start commit` row of `goal.md` section 4 as `| Phase start commit | Done | <the 40 character hash> |`. Verify: `grep -cE 'Phase start commit \| Done \| [0-9a-f]{40}' "$PHASE/goal.md"` prints `1`, `tail -1 "$PHASE/scratch/suite-before.txt"` starts with `exit=`, and `jq -e . "$PHASE/scratch/doctor-before.json" > /dev/null && echo DOCTOR_OK` prints `DOCTOR_OK`. The suite run takes several minutes.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:71:- [ ] T004 Save the 27 frozen rows (`scratch/audit/rows.jsonl`). Run the heredoc block that follows this line exactly as written. The file holds one JSON object per line with the fields `id`, `file`, `locator`, `expected_text`, `check` and `precheck`. The applier reads the first four and ignores the last two. Verify: the two commands under the block print `27` and then `27 1`. A line other than `27 1` means a `locator` no longer occurs exactly once in its file because the tree changed after this packet was written. Write that row id in `goal.md` section 4 and continue, because T006 reports the row as `BLOCKED`.
