specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:206:- [ ] T006 Apply the 27 rows, one at a time (`scratch/audit/applied.txt` and the 16 files the rows name). Run the block below. Do not edit any of those files by hand. Verify: the three counts under the block print `27`, `27` and `27`. A row that printed `BLOCKED` is recorded in `goal.md` section 4 and is not retried by hand. A row that printed `SKIP-MISSING` is recorded there with the pre-check that failed.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:229:  When a pre-check failed, the second and third counts are lower by the number of `SKIP-MISSING` rows. The gate is then `grep -c '^SKIP-MISSING ' "$PHASE/scratch/audit/applied.txt"` equals the number of missing artifacts in T001, and every skipped row is recorded in `goal.md` section 4.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:231:- [ ] T007 Rerun the four A1 to A4 searches and count the A5 references (`scratch/audit/searches.txt`). Run the block below. Verify: it prints `A1_rc=1`, `A2_rc=1`, `A3_rc=1`, `A4_rc=1` and `GUARD_REFS=6`. A code of 1 means ripgrep found nothing. A code of 0 means stale text is still there: read the saved search file, apply no hand edit, and mark this task `[B]`.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:238:  rg -n 'placeholder-upgrade: ".*block healthy-folder status' .skilled/commands > "$A/a2.txt" 2>&1; echo "A2_rc=$?" >> "$A/searches.txt"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:239:  rg -n -i '(^|[^a-z-])checklist\.md' .skilled/commands/speckit .skilled/agents > "$A/a3.txt" 2>&1; echo "A3_rc=$?" >> "$A/searches.txt"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:240:  rg -n 'level contract or manifest templates' .skilled/agents > "$A/a4.txt" 2>&1; echo "A4_rc=$?" >> "$A/searches.txt"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:241:  echo "GUARD_REFS=$(rg -l 'check-example-drift|check-card-sync' .skilled/commands/speckit .skilled/agents | wc -l | tr -d ' ')" >> "$A/searches.txt"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:245:- [ ] T008 Regenerate every mirror and run the eight checks (`scratch/mirrors/*.txt`, `scratch/mirrors/summary.txt`). Run the first block, then the second. The first block runs five generators in order and writes each one's output to its own file. The second block runs the eight read-only checks and records each exit code. Verify: `grep -c 'rc=0$' "$PHASE/scratch/mirrors/summary.txt"` prints `8`, and `grep -cE 'PASS|STATUS=OK|all mirrors in sync' "$PHASE/scratch/mirrors/summary.txt"` prints `8`, because the summary holds exactly one line per check. When a check exits 1, rerun its generator once and check again. A second failure marks this task `[B]`.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:272:- [ ] T009 Run the read-only doctor:speckit checks and compare the index staleness set (`scratch/doctor-after.json`, `scratch/index-before.json`, `scratch/index-after.json`). Run the block below. Verify: it prints `INDEX_STALENESS_SAME`, `gate1_exit=0` and `lookup_exit=0` or `lookup_exit=1`. An exit of 2 or higher from the lookup is an execution error, not a no-hit: mark this task `[B]`. `INDEX_STALENESS_DIFF` means this phase changed a document the index reads, which it must not: mark this task `[B]` and read the diff.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:281:  node "$S/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs" --check > "$PHASE/scratch/gate1.txt" 2>&1; echo "gate1_exit=$?"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:285:- [ ] T010 Check the phase 1 ledger rows owned by this phase (`scratch/audit/owner-006.tsv`, `scratch/audit/owner-006-open.txt`, `goal.md`). Run the block below. It prints `OWNER006=LEDGER_MISSING` when the ledger is absent. Otherwise it prints `OWNER006_TOTAL=<n>`, `OWNER006_OPEN=<m>`, one `COVERED` or `OPEN` line per owner `006` row and then `OWNER006_COUNTS_OK`. Verify: the block prints `OWNER006_COUNTS_OK`, so the status file matches both summary numbers. When the ledger is absent it prints `OWNER006=LEDGER_MISSING` instead and the task closes with it. Write both numbers and the path `scratch/audit/owner-006-open.txt` into the `Owner 006 ledger rows recorded (T010)` row of `goal.md` section 4. That file already holds every `OPEN` line verbatim, so no line is copied by hand. An `OPEN` row is not fixed here, because its text was not audited at authoring time. When `LED` is missing, write `OWNER006=LEDGER_MISSING` in the same row and the task closes with it.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:291:    echo "LEDGER_MISSING" > "$A/owner-006.tsv"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:292:    : > "$A/owner-006-open.txt"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:293:    echo "OWNER006=LEDGER_MISSING"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:295:    jq -r 'select(.owner_phase=="006") | [.id,.file] | @tsv' "$LED" > "$A/owner-006.tsv"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:299:    done < "$A/owner-006.tsv" > "$A/owner-006-status.txt"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:300:    grep '^OPEN ' "$A/owner-006-status.txt" > "$A/owner-006-open.txt" || :
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:301:    echo "OWNER006_TOTAL=$(wc -l < "$A/owner-006.tsv" | tr -d ' ')"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:302:    echo "OWNER006_OPEN=$(wc -l < "$A/owner-006-open.txt" | tr -d ' ')"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:303:    cat "$A/owner-006-status.txt"
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:304:    total_status=$(grep -cE '^(COVERED|OPEN) ' "$A/owner-006-status.txt")
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:305:    total_rows=$(grep -c . "$A/owner-006.tsv")
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment/tasks.md:306:    open_status=$(grep -c '^OPEN ' "$A/owner-006-status.txt")
