specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/003-versioned-placeholder-gate/tasks.md:1132:- [ ] T017 Run the whole spec-kit suite and compare it with the phase 1 start (`scratch/suite-end.txt`). Run the first block. It takes a long time: its duration is UNKNOWN until it runs, so give it up to the 10 minute bound per invocation that `runtime/scripts/run-tests.mjs` sets and read its output. Then run the second block. Verify: the second block prints `SUITE_MATCH_PLUS_NEW_TEST`. The compare tool accepts only a `Test Files` line that rose by 1 passed, a `Tests` line that rose by 5 passed, and an identical `exit=` line. Everything else must be identical. When it prints `SUITE_DIFF`, read the reason, read the lines of `suite-end.txt` that start with `FAIL` or hold `×`, and rerun the first block once before you decide, because a flaky test can differ between runs. A second `SUITE_DIFF` blocks the phase. Then run the third block and write its output in `goal.md` section 4: it shows whether the two `upgrade-level` suites changed, which is the ADR-006 probe.
