/bin/zsh -lc "rg -n --hidden -i 'intake[-_. ]lock|advisory lock|acquire.*lock|lock.*trio|with.*lock' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit" in /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/217-weak-model-spec-authoring
 succeeded in 0ms:
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md:71:- The block opens with `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` (exact case-sensitive heading, followed by colon). Indentation MAY be inside a markdown fenced code block or inline in the prompt text.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md:133:The `:confirm` mode (interactive, with full consolidated Q-block) is unaffected by this contract. Commands MUST preserve their existing `:confirm` behavior exactly. The contract applies ONLY when `execution_mode = AUTONOMOUS` (from `:auto` suffix or explicit `--mode=AUTONOMOUS` flag).
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md:147:Dispatch with exactly one ambiguous required field. Expected: ONE narrow question naming only that field; NEVER the full consolidated block.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md:153:Dispatch with `:confirm` suffix and any inputs. Expected: existing full consolidated Q-block emitted.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/grep-convention.md:122:| `malformed-or-unclosed` | An opening fence with no valid closing fence, or a block that does not parse | Skip, report, never partially rewrite |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/sub-folder-versioning.md:24:Enable clean separation of iterative work within a single spec folder while preserving historical context through packet continuity. Each iteration maintains its own canonical continuity (the `_memory.continuity` block in its `implementation-summary.md`) plus a git-ignored `scratch/` workspace tied to that child packet.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/execution-methods.md:102:The direct script acquires a packet-local `.canonical-save.lock` before mutating canonical continuity surfaces. A concurrent save fails fast while a stale lock older than the configured timeout is removed with a warning.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.1.5.0.md:15:Someone who does not care whether their spec folders match this repository's formats can now turn validation off once and keep working. `SPECKIT_SKIP_VALIDATION` used to trap commits: with it set, `validate.sh --json` printed nothing, so the pre-commit metadata gate read every staged packet as unreadable and blocked. A switched-off run now prints a report that says it skipped, and every local tool that reads that report counts the folder as skipped, never as passed.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/ux-hooks/directive-lifecycle-dedup.md:17:The skill-advisor brief carries a dynamic `Advisor:` route line followed by constant policy. Model-context runtimes send the complete block on the first proven turn and after lifecycle or transcript boundaries, then may retain only the route line on a proven repeat. When no brief exists the advisor hooks emit a fallback that opens with one status line above the directives block: `Advisor: outage (<label>); route by hand: ...`, `Advisor: no skill matched.` or `Advisor: prompt skipped.` Dedup treats that fallback like a brief, so a known, confirmed session gets the whole text on the first no-route turn and the status line alone on later turns, while unknown sessions, the kill switch and thrown errors always get the whole text. Pi's visible input transform instead suppresses its complete advisor-and-dispatch contribution on a proven repeat so the raw user turn remains byte-identical.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/ux-hooks/directive-lifecycle-dedup.md:41:   - OpenCode keeps an in-process mirror. Only one primitive, non-conflicting session identity can suppress. Ambiguous boundary events invalidate all older receipts. With the plugin's opt-in `deduplicateTransforms` on, the plugin hashes the full advisor block for same-message transform dedup before lifecycle reduction runs. Reduction runs only for a block that will be delivered, so dedup suppresses a repeated transform for the same message instead of delivering it as a shorter block.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md:494:The pointer is maintained automatically by the generator: a save into a child points every phase-parent ancestor one level down toward it. A save aimed at a phase parent moves the pointers only when a `--full-auto` save routes its continuity into a leaf, and otherwise moves none. A track root keeps its pointer in the telemetry store only. Atomic write via temp+rename. No `_memory.continuity` block exists at a phase parent (per the lean trio policy — parents have no `implementation-summary.md`).
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md:3:description: Canonical spec-folder intake contract shared by /speckit:plan and /speckit:complete. Defines folder classification, repair-mode routing, staged trio publication, relationship capture, resume semantics, and the intake lock.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md:10:  - "intake lock"
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md:77:| Preflight | Inspect + classify folder; acquire advisory intake lock | `spec_path`, `folder_state` (caller-local), `start_state` (canonical), `repair_mode`, `resume_question_id`, `reentry_reason` |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md:102:| `partial-folder` | Folder exists, trio incomplete, no tracked seed markers, no intake lock | `repair-metadata` |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md:203:## 9. INTAKE LOCK
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md:205:An advisory lock file prevents concurrent trio publication on the same folder.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md:210:- Stale lock (older than a conservative timeout): surface exact cleanup command (`rm <path>.intake.lock`)
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md:236:| Stale or contended intake lock | Fail closed (STATUS=FAIL) with exact cleanup or retry guidance |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md:273:- Intake lock acquired at Phase 1 entry, released at Phase 3 exit (or on cancel)
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.1.0.0.md:33:- **Old spec folders upgrade in one command.** A tool with no language model fills what v1 documents lack and records the findings it cannot clear, so strict validation passes and old debt stops blocking new work.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.1.0.0.md:54:For each active packet that fails, it fills in the frontmatter keys (the metadata block at the top of each document) a document lacks without rewriting any value already there. A document whose metadata block it cannot read is left as it is, and the run names it. It then runs the existing repair tools on the packet and writes every finding they cannot clear into the packet's `upgrade-baseline.json`.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.1.0.0.md:58:The same work tightens the backfill that regenerates a packet's derived metadata. It exits with a failure when a folder cannot be re-derived, so the repair tool reports the failure instead of calling the packet repaired. The pre-commit hook therefore blocks a commit whose metadata cannot be re-derived.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/agent-io-contract.md:190:- The group is optional. A record that omits the evidence metadata entirely is valid and passes post-dispatch validation with no warning (absence never blocks).
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/debugging/troubleshooting.md:134:| **Orphan marker** | An opening marker with no closing pair | Report it as a diagnostic; do not silently drop the block |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v1+/v1.7.0.0.md:170:The local embedding provider remains degraded with its retry circuit breaker open, blocking a `parentChain` index refresh until the provider recovers. A `validate.sh` global-index-reconciliation preventive is deferred to a later cycle.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v1+/v1.7.0.0.md:268:Before accepting a STOP for lack of new ground, deep-research compares the run's novelty report with graph-observed changes to stored questions, findings and evidence. It blocks a stop the graph cannot support.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v1+/v1.7.0.0.md:324:Lexical grounding, noise-floor subtraction, evidence-gap handling, relevance-aware warnings and calibrated scores run on with the cite-with-caveat tier, the envelope-fidelity guard, spec-metadata integrity gates and the false-confirm build gate. The type-safe status validator runs in a non-blocking report mode during the migration window before it enforces.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.7.1.0.md:98:The pre-commit check compares the trigger phrases of each staged Markdown file with its committed version, and it grades only the phrases you added. A template-default or editor-fallback phrase blocks the commit, and the block message names the bypass. Other negative classes only print a warning. If the linter, `node` or git is unavailable, the check warns and lets the commit through. The phrase cleanup now covers all 18 template kinds, writes each file atomically and routes a file without frontmatter to the fixer instead of counting it as skipped.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.7.1.0.md:102:The changed-packet gate validates each packet that fails at the head, then validates the same packet at the merge base with the same validator. It blocks only on rules that the head fails and the base does not. A report it cannot read counts as a failure, so the gate fails closed. The weekly sweep now downloads the previous successful run's report as its baseline. A folder that passed in that baseline and fails now is marked as a regression. With no previous report, the run records a baseline and reports no error.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/context-preservation/session-relaunch-loop.md:53:The killer polls transcript modification time every 100 ms. Once the transcript is idle, it confirms that the target descends from the loop and re-reads the record. It sends SIGTERM only when the record is armed. Before a signal it re-checks the hop cap: a record at the cap is un-armed with reason `hop-cap`, logged as `killer-hop-cap` and left unsignalled with no notification, because no relaunch would follow and the manual claim is already the session's own instruction. Without a transcript it treats elapsed idle time since start as the idle signal. In OpenCode's Bun-hosted plugin, the detached killer runs with node because process.execPath points to the OpenCode CLI. A single failed transcript read does not end supervision. The killer gives up only after the transcript has stayed unreadable for 1 s without a break. That give-up re-reads the record first. When a later prepare armed a different note, it leaves that record alone and logs `killer-timeout-superseded` with the `watched` and `current` note paths. Otherwise it un-arms the record with reason killer-timeout and attempts the notification. Taking over a stale killer lock goes through a takeover mutex that records its owner pid. The mutex is reclaimed when that owner is dead. It is also reclaimed once it has outlived the longest hold a real holder needs. A mutex with no owner file is reclaimed once it is older than 30 s.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/save-workflow.md:245:| `completion_pct`     | integer | 0 to 100, and 100 only with no blockers or open questions |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/save-workflow.md:297:| Locked | The packet-local `.canonical-save.lock` is acquired before any canonical continuity file is mutated. Parallel saves against the same folder fail fast; a lock whose owner process is gone is reclaimed with a warning. Together this keeps simultaneous handoff writes from interleaving. |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/save-workflow.md:330:- **At a phase parent**: the parent holds no `implementation-summary.md`, so a `--full-auto` save carrying continuity fields resolves the leaf that holds the work and writes there. At each level, payload paths (`filesModified` and `key_files`) that lie inside a child choose that child when they all name the same one. A level with no such path follows its `derived.last_active_child_id` pointer when the pointer names an existing child packet. Payload paths spread across two children, or no path and no usable pointer, resolve nothing: the save writes no continuity, names the candidate children, and leaves every pointer unchanged. The routed leaf is written under its own `.canonical-save.lock` and its graph metadata is refreshed in the same save. Logic: `resolveContinuityLeaf` in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/continuity/generate-context.ts`.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md:296:`create.sh` rejects `--path` values that traverse outside the repository with a clear error before any write. Set `SPECKIT_POST_VALIDATE=1` when a strict workflow should run full validation immediately after scaffolding. A mkdir-based advisory lock protects `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` writes during canonical save so two parallel `/speckit:save` calls for the same packet do not race.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v1+/v1.4.2.0.md:98:Every write to the spec-memory MCP failed with `SQLITE_CONSTRAINT_PRIMARYKEY`, which blocked `memory_save`, `memory_index_scan` and `memory_match_triggers`. The spec-memory daemon could not index or save.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/ux-hooks/goal-opencode-plugin.md:77:goal_prompt="Role: Focused OpenCode execution agent operating under the active session goal.\nObjective: Finish the goal plugin docs integration and validate it\nContext: Use the current conversation, repository files, tests, and active spec constraints as source of truth. Preserve unrelated worktree changes and do not broaden scope.\nMethod:\n- Restate the concrete completion condition from available evidence before acting.\n- Clarify the concrete completion condition from available context, then execute until it is met or blocked.\n- Prefer direct, reversible changes; ask only when blocked by missing information, permissions, or contradictory requirements.\nSuccess Criteria:\n- The requested outcome is materially complete, not merely analyzed or partially prepared.\n- Required verification has run, or any inability to run it is reported with the exact blocker.\n- Status output distinguishes confirmed evidence from inference.\nStop Conditions:\n- Stop only when the goal verifier can mark the goal met, when the user changes or clears the goal, or when progress is blocked by a decision the user must make.\n- If blocked, preserve state and name the next safe action."
