.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-deep-loop_036-deep-loop-innovation_007-executor-and-cli-hardening_010-fanout-write-containment-hardening_010-containment-on-failed-lanes_spec.md:82:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs` | Modify | Containment moved into the post-process lifecycle step, ahead of log saving, salvage and every verdict gate; `containmentFindings` still feeds only the post-gate advisory status |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-deep-loop_036-deep-loop-innovation_007-executor-and-cli-hardening_010-fanout-write-containment-hardening_010-containment-on-failed-lanes_spec.md:102:| REQ-003 | A complete lane's advisory path is unchanged |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-deep-loop_036-deep-loop-innovation_007-executor-and-cli-hardening_010-fanout-write-containment-hardening_010-containment-on-failed-lanes_spec.md:155:- Complete lane with a stray write: advisory as before
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-deep-loop_036-deep-loop-innovation_007-executor-and-cli-hardening_010-fanout-write-containment-hardening_013-review-lane-advisory-and-strict-config_spec.md:2:title: "Feature Specification: Phase 6: review-lane-advisory-and-strict-config"
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-deep-loop_036-deep-loop-innovation_007-executor-and-cli-hardening_010-fanout-write-containment-hardening_013-review-lane-advisory-and-strict-config_spec.md:3:description: "The empty-registry advisory reads the registry field of the loop it inspects, so review lanes with open findings no longer misfire, and the fan-out containment schema rejects an unknown key such as the removed worktrees option by name."
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-deep-loop_036-deep-loop-innovation_007-executor-and-cli-hardening_010-fanout-write-containment-hardening_013-review-lane-advisory-and-strict-config_spec.md:5:  - "review lane advisory and strict config"
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-deep-loop_036-deep-loop-innovation_007-executor-and-cli-hardening_010-fanout-write-containment-hardening_013-review-lane-advisory-and-strict-config_spec.md:6:  - "the empty registry advisory reads the registry field"
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-deep-loop_036-deep-loop-innovation_007-executor-and-cli-hardening_010-fanout-write-containment-hardening_013-review-lane-advisory-and-strict-config_spec.md:11:# Feature Specification: Phase 6: review-lane-advisory-and-strict-config
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-deep-loop_036-deep-loop-innovation_007-executor-and-cli-hardening_010-fanout-write-containment-hardening_013-review-lane-advisory-and-strict-config_spec.md:58:The empty-registry advisory checked `keyFindings` for every loop type, but a review registry carries `openFindings`, so both lanes of the ten-iteration review, holding 24 and 8 open findings, raised `lineage_registry_empty`. Separately, the containment schema was a plain object, so a config still carrying the removed `worktrees` key passed silently.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-deep-loop_036-deep-loop-innovation_007-executor-and-cli-hardening_010-fanout-write-containment-hardening_013-review-lane-advisory-and-strict-config_spec.md:61:The advisory fires only when a lane truly registered nothing, and a stale config key fails loudly with its name.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-deep-loop_036-deep-loop-innovation_007-executor-and-cli-hardening_010-fanout-write-containment-hardening_013-review-lane-advisory-and-strict-config_spec.md:75:- The advisory's delta counting - unchanged
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-deep-loop_036-deep-loop-innovation_007-executor-and-cli-hardening_010-fanout-write-containment-hardening_013-review-lane-advisory-and-strict-config_spec.md:84:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/fanout-run.vitest.ts` | Modify | Two new advisory tests |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-deep-loop_036-deep-loop-innovation_007-executor-and-cli-hardening_010-fanout-write-containment-hardening_013-review-lane-advisory-and-strict-config_spec.md:175:| Risk | 6/25 | Advisory and config parsing |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-speckit_z_archive_022-hybrid-rag-fusion_009-perfect-session-capturing_016-json-mode-hybrid-enrichment_004-indexing-and-coherence_spec.md:212:- Pre-save overlap MCP query times out: Log warning, continue save — overlap detection is advisory not blocking
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/fixtures/anchor-repair-sample/specs_system-speckit_z_archive_022-hybrid-rag-fusion_009-perfect-session-capturing_016-json-mode-hybrid-enrichment_004-indexing-and-coherence_spec.md:292:- Does the pre-save overlap check (REQ-012) need to be synchronous for the first save of a spec folder, or advisory-only across all saves? (Recommend advisory-only to keep P2 scope contained)
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lib/corpus.mjs:78: * fail-closed gate quietly becomes advisory. The exemption covers the refusal
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lib/grep-convention.mjs:144:/** Canonical frontmatter keys, in the order a created block writes them. */
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/README.md:84:`generate-trigger-index.mjs --check` says whether an index still matches the corpus. It walks and reads the corpus as a build does and compares each document's declared phrases with the phrases the index attributes to it, the same comparison the save path runs for one packet (`lib/freshness.mjs`). It also counts index paths the corpus no longer holds. It writes nothing and exits `0` when nothing differs, `1` when a document is stale, an index path is obsolete or the corpus is untrusted, and `2` on a bad invocation or an unreadable index. A manifest hash that differs while every phrase matches is printed as a note and does not fail the check. It costs one full corpus walk, so it runs as the report-only `advisory-checks.yml` step and by hand, never per lookup.
